    "question": "Kim has 4 dozen shirts.  She lets her sister have 1/3 of them.  How many shirts does she have left?",
    "gold": "32",
    "answer": "She had 4*12=<<4*12=48>>48 shirts to start with\nShe gives away 48/3=<<48/3=16>>16\nSo she has 48-16=<<48-16=32>>32 left\n#### 32"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many shirts Kim has left after letting her sister have 1/3 of them, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of shirts Kim initially has.\n   Kim has 4 dozen shirts. Since one dozen equals 12 shirts, we can calculate the total number of shirts as follows:\n   \\[\n   4 \\times 12 = 48\n   \\]\n   So, Kim initially has 48 shirts.\n\n2. Determine how many shirts Kim's sister gets.\n   Kim's sister gets 1/3 of the 48 shirts. To find out how many shirts this is, we calculate:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{3} \\times 48 = 16\n   \\]\n   So, Kim's sister gets 16 shirts.\n\n3. Calculate how many shirts Kim has left.\n   To find out how many shirts Kim has left, we subtract the number of shirts her sister got from the total number of shirts Kim initially had:\n   \\[\n   48 - 16 = 32\n   \\]\n   So, Kim has 32 shirts left.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{32}\n\\]",
